{
  "about": "U27 caves: refinements of the baseline (tools/sounds/baseline/caves.json). Original sound designs; upstream's audio is never read. The events (ids, subtitles, categories, volumes, pitches, variant counts) stay upstream's; as in upstream the Yeti plays the Alpha Yeti's files (upstream plays them at its own pitch). The yetis are big furred beasts in an ice cave: deep wobbling growls with a frosty breath, a short barking roar when they take notice, a huge rising roar, heavy panting, a grunt and a thump as they grab, a swung whoosh with an effort grunt when they throw, and a long roar that sinks into the cave's echo when they die. The Troll grumbles in slow, low syllables over a throat rumble, grunts with a rock scrape as it grabs a rock, heaves the rock with a whoosh, and dies with a long groan and the thump of its fall.",
